From de29b4c012ec5b00aaf9924c08e594d251e507a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] session writes ride out a starting gateway instead
 of a 503 telling the user to stop it

Hub, Nov 13: two Desktop archive PATCHes sent 4 s and 10 s after a gateway restart came back
503 `owner_unavailable: starting: Exclusive maintenance refused: Gateway runtime already owns
profile ... Drain and stop the gateway, then retry.` The same request 15-30 s later landed.

Five whys
1. Owner discovery answered `starting`: the new gateway held the profile lock but had not
   published READY.
2. `discover_session_owner` re-read only `inaccessible/control_timeout`; `starting` was final
   on the first read.
3. With no endpoint the write went to the offline store, lost the lock to the starting gateway,
   and `owner_unavailable_detail` appended the offline lock's remedy.
4. That remedy is wrong for a gateway that is only starting: nothing was written and the edit
   only has to be sent again (or wait a few seconds).
5. Not caught: the control_timeout tests never exercised a write during gateway startup, and
   three tests pinned `starting` as a first-read refusal.

Fix
- `starting` (no endpoint) is re-read, read-only, every 0.5 s on its own budget of 24 s from the
  first read. Measured on the hub over 97 starts in 36 h, from systemd start: control socket
  8.3 s median, READY 22.1 s median / 25.2 s p90. Desktop cuts a request at 30 s, so 24 s leaves
  the forward its own time. Once `starting` was seen, a missed identify deadline of the busy
  starting loop is re-read on the same deadline. The mutation is still sent at most once and
  discovery never starts a gateway.
- A gateway still starting at the deadline answers the retryable 503
  `owner_unavailable: starting: the gateway that owns this profile is starting; nothing was
  changed, retry`, without drain/stop advice.
- `absent`, draining and every refusal verdict stay final on the first read with their details.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_session_owner_discovery_starting.py (18; 17 fail without the fix),
including a real gateway frozen while starting whose write lands exactly once, and a real lock
reservation that is refused in budget with nothing changed. Three tests that pinned the old
`starting` refusal now assert the new detail (or use `draining` for the unchanged path).
